    "created_at": "2025-03-25T15:10:38Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-03-25T15:10:38Z",
    "body": "what would the expectations be for if this was allowed?  replacing the current textarea entry entirely with the chosen option?  inserting the chosen option's value at the current location of the text cursor?\n\nfor single-line inputs, down arrow is commonly used to navigate to and through the datalist's options - but down arrow in a multi-line text area is meant to move the text entry cursor to the next line(s).  So, a new keyboard command to move to a datalist's options would need to be defined by user agents/operating systems for how to consistently allow access.\n\nmy comment is not meant to be a full response to the ask of \"why\" but merely the immediate things that come to mind for how this would work.",
