    "created_at": "2026-02-01T23:02:51Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-02-01T23:02:51Z",
    "body": ">inserting the chosen option's value at the current location of the text cursor?\n\nThis would be great for hypermedia-driven frameworks like html: The developer does not have to write code that writes to the textarea, but can just use the textarea's current state (text, cursor position) to calculate a set of completion candidataes which are appropriate for the current state, and the browser will do the rest.\n\n> replacing the current textarea entry entirely with the chosen option?\n\nThis is probably also great for some usecases, being able to select one of the two with an html attribute would probably suit all.\n",
